# The game is committed whole - engine, data, art, audio, fonts and effects -
# so that a clone of this repository is a game you can run, with nothing to
# fetch from anywhere else. That costs about 100MB, which is the price of the
# thing being self-contained.

# Saved games belong to whoever is playing, not to the game.
/save/

# Build output: packaged applications and the screenshots the scenarios take.
/dist/
/build/scenarios/*.png
/build/scenarios/logs/

# Notes from one session to the next, so that a cleared context can pick the
# work up. It is scaffolding for whoever is building the game, not part of the
# game, and it is rewritten wholesale every time - committing it would put a
# stale set of instructions in the history and a merge conflict in the way of
# every branch.
/build/RESTART.md

__pycache__/
*.pyc
